Package: pulzr-ip
Maintainer: Joseph Telaak <joseph@pulzr.net>
License: Apache-2.0
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: pulzr-base
Description: Requests to devices on the gateway's LAN for their codecs.
 A device that speaks its own protocol over IP (an IP camera's settings API)
 is driven by its device type's codec in Pulzr, which turns each command into
 HTTP, TCP or UDP requests; pulzr-edge-ip makes them, against that device's
 address on the LAN and nothing else. Nothing device-specific is on the
 gateway. In every image with LAN ports (PACKAGES_LAN). Built from
 github.com/pulzar-net/pulzr-edge with the OpenWrt SDK, with its ip feature
 alone; see sdk/packages/pulzr-edge.
